class:: FeatureSmooth
summary:: One-pole smoothing at feature update instants
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Lag, Classes/FeatureMedian, Classes/FeatureDelta

description::
Updates y = exp(-frameTime/time)*previous + (1-exp(-frameTime/time))*input at accepted update instants. The first accepted value initializes the state directly. time is the 1/e settling constant, unlike the 60 dB lag-time convention used by vanilla Lag.

A negative trigger accepts every control block. A nonnegative trigger accepts only positive edges and holds the output between edges; this lets the caller align updates with analysis frames. frameTime must match that regular update spacing. Irregular triggers do not create a nonuniform regression. Nonfinite input is replaced by zero. Cost and state are constant. This is an independent one-pole low-pass recurrence. Vanilla Lag has a related purpose, while this UGen can update only when a feature frame arrives and uses a 1/e time constant.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Control-rate or scalar feature, with multichannel expansion for feature arrays.

argument:: time
Nonnegative 1/e smoothing time in seconds; zero bypasses smoothing.

argument:: trigger
Negative: update every control block. Otherwise update on positive edges.

argument:: frameTime
Seconds between accepted values. Zero uses the server control period; supply the actual period when triggering sparsely.

returns::
Smoothed input value.

examples::
FeatureSmooth performs causal one-pole exponential smoothing calibrated in physical seconds. In this example, it processes spectral flux extracted from a bowing friction texture: fast fluctuations are integrated into a slow, organic swell parameter that smoothly breathes open the wet space of an algorithmic reverb. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: plots the smoothed feature trajectory.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("texture.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic texture fallback
            PinkNoise.ar * LFNoise1.kr(1).range(0.2, 0.8) + SinOsc.ar(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(200, 800), 0, 0.2)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var flux = FFTFlux2.kr(chain, fftSize: 1024);
        var smoothedFlux = FeatureSmooth.kr(flux, time: 0.2, trigger: -1, frameTime: 0.01);
        var revSize = smoothedFlux.linlin(0.0, 0.4, 0.1, 0.95).clip(0.1, 0.98);
        var verb = FreeVerb.ar(source, 0.7, revSize, 0.5) * 0.4;
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + verb;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, smoothedFlux) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Smoothed Feature", ~miraBus, 0.0, 0.5);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
